<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="6142cb66-beff-5091-a3b5-1868c6419e4a" activityNameId="f8c61c1b-ace0-513a-98a4-1417aa4c3611" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation system, centralized, average for 6 m3(hm2)</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation system, centralized, average for 6 m3(hm2)
Disposal of a ventilation system for a building with a specific air flow rate of 6 m3/h per m2 heated gross floor area. The reference value of the inventory is 1 m2 heated gross floor area. The inventory is based on average data of 4 office buildings, 3 schools and 3 residential care homes with a total heated gross floor area of 61719 m2 and a total nominal air flow of 302190 m3/h, specific weight of the components: 11.4 kg/m2, including average components for air handling units, ducts including insulation, air valves, roof-hoods, dampers, fire dampers, silencers. The data represent a ductwork mainly made of galvanized steel and includes air handling units mainly with heat recovery and a nominal air flow rate of 5'000-20'000 m3/h per unit. No ground heat exchanger is included.;
UUID: 0fdc2e7e-1c8b-4337-a15a-de11b03799ac
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0fdc2e7e-1c8b-4337-a15a-de11b03799ac.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">CH</shortname>
